---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | SaveFileTool"
  description="Read how SaveFileTool handles local RPG Maker save files, browser storage, and support messages."
>
  <section class="container mx-auto px-4 py-12 max-w-4xl">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold mb-8 text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <div class="prose prose-blue max-w-none dark:prose-invert">
      <p class="text-lg text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300 mb-8">
        <strong>Last Updated:</strong> September 29, 2026
      </p>

      <section class="mb-10">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">1. Overview</h2>
        <p>
          SaveFileTool is a browser-side RPG Maker save editor. The current public build does not
          ship third-party analytics scripts, advertising scripts, or server-side save parsing.
        </p>
        <div class="bg-blue-50 dark:bg-blue-900/20 border-l-4 border-blue-500 p-4 my-6">
          <p class="font-bold text-blue-800 dark:text-blue-200">Key Takeaway:</p>
          <p class="text-blue-700 dark:text-blue-300">
            Selected save files are read in your browser. Optional history and templates are stored
            in your browser's IndexedDB only when you enable or save them.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-10">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">2. Information You Provide</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-4">
          <li>
            <strong>Save files:</strong> Files you choose are loaded by the browser for editing.
            They are not sent to a SaveFileTool server by the editor flow.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Optional local history:</strong> If enabled, original and edited files are kept
            in your browser's IndexedDB for faster repeat edits. You can disable and clear this
            history from the editor.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Optional local templates:</strong> Saved edit templates are stored in your
            browser's IndexedDB for reuse on the same device.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Support messages:</strong> If you email us, your email address and message are
            used to respond to your request.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-10">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">3. Automatically Processed Data</h2>
        <p>
          Hosting and security providers may process standard request data, such as IP address,
          browser type, requested URL, timestamp, and basic security signals. This is used to serve
          the website and protect it from abuse.
        </p>
        <p>
          The current public build does not include third-party analytics, advertising scripts,
          cross-site ad cookies, or a first-party analytics beacon.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-10">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">4. How We Use Information</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6">
          <li>To operate and maintain the website.</li>
          <li>To run the browser-side editor on files you choose.</li>
          <li>To provide optional local history and templates.</li>
          <li>To answer support requests you send by email.</li>
          <li>To protect the site from malicious activity and abuse.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-10">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">5. Your Choices</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6">
          <li>You can use the editor without creating an account.</li>
          <li>You can choose not to enable local history.</li>
          <li>You can clear local history and templates from your browser storage.</li>
          <li>You can contact us to delete support messages you previously sent.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-10">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">6. Children's Privacy</h2>
        <p>
          The service is not directed to children under 13. We do not knowingly collect personal
          information from children.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-10">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">7. Changes to This Policy</h2>
        <p>
          We may update this Privacy Policy by posting a new version on this page and updating the
          "Last Updated" date.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-10">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">8. Contact Us</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about privacy can be sent to
          <a href="mailto:privacy@savefiletool.com" class="text-primary-600 hover:underline"
            >privacy@savefiletool.com</a
          >.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </section>
  <script type="application/ld+json">
    {
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "WebPage",
      "name": "Privacy Policy",
      "url": "https://savefiletool.com/privacy",
      "description": "Privacy Policy for SaveFileTool.",
      "lastReviewed": "2026-09-29",
      "specialty": "LegalDocument"
    }
  </script>
</BaseLayout>
